WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.840
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. It's take your brother to work day.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:04.620
Oh look!

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.800
There you are! Right in the entryway.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.160
So you walk in, first thing you see is the crash course posters

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.200
and some foreign editions of The Fault In Our Stars.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.400
And then you see Danica's Mac

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.920
with it's wiggly eyes

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.300
and Danica herself, hi Danica

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:17.830
[Danica]: Hello

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.960
This area is for the visitors we don't have.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:20.789
Danica works on Crash Course.

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:23.340
She does all those chalkboard drawings that are so excellent

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:25.140
and also the Mental Floss set.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.300
Then you come to our printer room where Wil Wheaton and Felicia Day

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.440
have the place of honor,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.280
and then you spin around and look, oh, it's Meredith!

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.480
Who doesn't want to be on TV today.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.520
Meredith writes for Mental Floss,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.000
but more importantly,

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.020
is the CEO of the Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.080
And then we come to my office.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:43.340
Oh hi, there Buster, scared of sheep.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.060
This is my couch.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:47.740
This is the lazy boy where I've written at least parts of every single one of my books

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.600
And this is the treadmill desk where I have taken

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.400
360 whole steps today.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.620
Oh, and what?

00:00:52.629 --> 00:00:54.740
A signed Pelé jersey that says

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:56.660
"To J. Green, DFTBA, good luck, Pelé."

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:57.200
Whaaat?

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.520
This is the television where the Swindon Town Swoodilypoopers come to life,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.640
and this is a painting by Sarah.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.680
So Hank, before Sarah and I started dating, I actually bought that painting from her

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.980
and then months later,

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:09.390
when she came over to my apartment for the first time while we were dating, I was like,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.520
"Look, I framed your beautiful painting!"

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:12.209
And she said, "Yeah,

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:12.980
That's upside-down."

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:14.780
Sometimes people ask me for romantic advice,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:15.680
my advice?

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.800
Hang your future girlfriend's painting right-side up, for God's sakes.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.100
I also keep all my foreign editions of The Fault In Our Stars here like,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.500
"Das Schicksal Ist Ein Mieser Verräter"

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.420
"Förr Eller Senare Exploderar Jag",

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:27.780
"Faen Ta Skjebnen",

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.180
"Tähtiin kirjoitettu virhe",

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.720
then of course, there's "Gwiazd Nasych Wina",

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.940
"Nos Étoiles Contraires"

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.220
(I actually took French.)

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:37.120
...And the ones I have no way of  even pretending to know how to attempt.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:37.880
Also in my office,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.210
we have Leonardo's Leonardo.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.160
But most importantly, we have this beautiful view of the river, including

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.380
Canada Geese.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.000
I used to say Canadian Geese, Hank.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.980
But then Canadians informed me, politely,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.020
that that is incorrect.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.040
"Geese don't have a nationality!", they said. "Thank you for mentioning Canada."

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.600
Baby ducks, baby ducks, baby ducks,

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:53.640
duckieeees!

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.460
Then we go down the hall and we have the kitchen,

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:58.400
featuring artwork by my lovely son, Henry Green,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.580
as well as posters available now at &lt;dftba.com&gt;

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.700
We have to keep all the clif bars in here because mice.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.680
Here is the tiger who does all the dishes.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:07.580
Thanks tiger!

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:10.120
This is apparently the jar where we keep all the action figures,

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.740
you know so they don't get out and wreak havoc.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.200
This is the room where we shoot Mental Floss where Stan and Mark also work?

00:02:15.209 --> 00:02:16.740
There's the mental floss set.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.740
Mark's the producer and director of the Mental Floss channel, say hi, Mark.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.120
[Mark]: Hi, Mark.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:23.920
And Stan, of course, is working on Crash Course as he always is.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.020
[Stan]: Hi.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.040
[Stan]: Stan.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.140
Since this is an episode of Cribs, I got to show you what's in our fridge.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:31.180
Mostly soda

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.800
and some beer

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.900
and apples!

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.100
Good job everybody.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.480
Also, Hank, I have a theory that you'll find mustard in any refrigerator

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:40.040
and sure enough, even though we have nothing to mustard,

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:40.760
mustard.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.240
So Hank, I wanted you to see the office

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.840
because 1) you've showed me yours

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.040
and 2) I wanted you to be able to meet

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:51.299
all of the nice people who actually make Crash Course and Mental Floss and the Swoodilypoopers happen.

00:02:51.299 --> 00:02:52.920
This is particularly important because soon

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:53.940
I will be on Paternity leave.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.760
But the things that we make here will continue to be made, even though I will not be in the office.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.780
By the way I just noticed th- I- the pizza- me- red- why- hmm- yeah?

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.760
I'm gonna go down here by the thing that isn't a mustache.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:07.109
So Hank, the Yeti's due to have a baby on June 1st

00:03:07.109 --> 00:03:09.840
but it might happen earlier because you know that's- that's the way with babies.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.300
So hopefully you'll see me next Tuesday,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.840
but I will definitely see you on Friday.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:13.700
DFTBA.

